Implementation Plan:
1) Conceptual Model & Pattern Guidance

**Concept:** `:DocumentSection`
**Represents:** A numbered section or appendix within the product specification document, identified by its heading text and section number.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use the **Tree** pattern to represent the hierarchical nesting of sections (e.g., 8.3.1 is a child of 8.3). Use the **Name Stub** pattern to capture the section heading as a simple string label.
**Key Relationships:** `:hasParentSection` (to parent `:DocumentSection`), `:sectionNumber` (xsd:string), `:sectionTitle` (xsd:string). A `:DocumentSection` `:describes` a `:owl:Thing` (the concept it covers).

**Concept:** `:ServiceAttribute`
**Represents:** A set of service-level attributes for a specific interface or component (e.g., UNI-D, CVC, NNI).
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Property Reification** to model the `:ServiceAttribute` as a class that groups individual attribute values. Use **Explicit Typing** to create subclasses for each specific attribute set (e.g., `:UniDServiceAttribute`, `:CvcServiceAttribute`).
**Key Relationships:** `:isAttributeOf` (to the entity it describes, e.g., `:AVC`, `:CVC`, `:NNIGroup`), `:hasAttributeValue` (to a reified value or literal).

**Concept:** `:OrderableAttribute`
**Represents:** A set of attributes that can be specified when ordering a product component (e.g., NNI Bearer, NNI Link, V-NNI).
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Property Reification** to model the `:OrderableAttribute` as a class. Use **Explicit Typing** to create subclasses for each specific orderable attribute set (e.g., `:NniBearerOrderableAttribute`, `:NniLinkOrderableAttribute`).
**Key Relationships:** `:isAttributeOf` (to the orderable entity, e.g., `:Bearer`, `:NNILink`), `:hasAttributeValue` (to a reified value or literal).

2) Reuse & Extension Plan

**Extend/Reuse:**
- `:NNIGroup` (reuse as-is for NNI Group entity)
- `:Bearer` (reuse as-is for NNI Bearer entity)
- `:NNILink` (reuse as-is for NNI Link / V-NNI entity)
- `:AVC` (reuse as-is for AVC entity)
- `:CVC` (reuse as-is for CVC entity)
- `:OrderableAttribute` (reuse existing extension class)
- `:ServiceAttribute` (reuse existing extension class)
- `:sectionNumber` (reuse existing extension datatype property)

**Create New:**
- `:DocumentSection` (class) – represents a numbered section heading in the document.
- `:hasParentSection` (object property) – links a subsection to its parent section.
- `:sectionTitle` (datatype property, xsd:string) – the heading text of a section.
- `:describes` (object property) – links a `:DocumentSection` to the concept it describes.
- `:isAttributeOf` (object property) – links an attribute set (ServiceAttribute, OrderableAttribute) to the entity it describes.
- `:UniDServiceAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for UNI-D service attributes.
- `:UniDslServiceAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for UNI-DSL service attributes.
- `:UnicastAvcServiceAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for Unicast AVC service attributes.
- `:CvcServiceAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for CVC service attributes.
- `:NniServiceAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for NNI service attributes.
- `:NniGroupLocationAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for NNI Group Location.
- `:NniGroupInterfaceRateAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for NNI Group Interface Rate.
- `:NniGroupRedundancyModeAttribute` (class, subclass of `:ServiceAttribute`) – for NNI Group Redundancy Mode.
- `:NniGroupOrderableAttributesSummary` (class, subclass of `:OrderableAttribute`) – for NNI Group Orderable Attributes Summary.
- `:NniBearerOrderableAttribute` (class, subclass of `:OrderableAttribute`) – for NNI Bearer Orderable Attributes.
- `:NniLinkOrderableAttribute` (class, subclass of `:OrderableAttribute`) – for NNI Link Orderable Attributes.
- `:VNniOrderableAttribute` (class, subclass of `:OrderableAttribute`) – for V-NNI Orderable Attributes.
- `:ModificationEvent` (class) – for the event of modifying an AVC bandwidth profile.
- `:AccessTechnologyCompatibility` (class) – for the appendix on access technology compatibility.
- `:TrafficClassCombinations` (class) – for the appendix on traffic class combinations.

