Implementation Plan:
1) Conceptual Model & Pattern Guidance

**Concept:** `Cl_TrafficClass`
**Represents:** A class of traffic (TC-1, TC-2, TC-4) with specific performance attributes and specifications (CIR or PIR) for allocating service capacity.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use `Explicit Typing` to define each traffic class as an individual of `:TrafficClass`. Use `Property Reification` to model the `hasSpecification` relationship, as it is context-dependent (e.g., TC-4 has different specifications at AVC vs. CVC). Use `Stubs` for the `hasExampleApplication` and `alignedTo` relationships, as these are descriptive text values rather than complex entities.
**Key Relationships:** `:consumes` (from CVC), `:hasSpecification` (reified, to CIR/PIR), `:hasExampleApplication` (to text), `:alignedTo` (to DSCP PHB), `:hasBurstCapability` (to text), `:capacitySharing` (reified, to text with context).

**Concept:** `Cl_InformationRateSpecification`
**Represents:** The specification type (CIR or PIR) applied to a traffic class at a specific network point (AVC or CVC), with contextual qualifiers.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use `Property Reification` to create a reification class that captures the `hasSpecification` relationship with its qualifiers (`when`, `unless`). This is essential because the same traffic class (TC-4) can have different specification types depending on the network point (AVC vs. CVC) and network type (Satellite vs. other).
**Key Relationships:** `:specifiesTrafficClass` (to `Cl_TrafficClass`), `:specifiesRateType` (to CIR/PIR), `:appliesAt` (to AVC/CVC), `:appliesToNetwork` (to Satellite/other), `:hasSpecification` (from TrafficClass).

**Concept:** `Cl_NetworkPoint`
**Represents:** The network interface or circuit where a traffic class specification applies (AVC, CVC, UNI, NNI).
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use `Explicit Typing` to define AVC, CVC, UNI, and NNI as individuals of their respective classes. Use `Partonymy/Meronymy` to model the relationship between AVC and CVC (AVC uses CVC), and between CVC and NNI Group (CVC maps to NNI Group).
**Key Relationships:** `:usesCvc` (AVC to CVC), `:mapsTo` (CVC to NNIGroup), `:terminatesAtPoi` (NNIGroup to POI), `:hasSpecification` (reified, from TrafficClass).

2) Reuse & Extension Plan

**Extend/Reuse:**
- `:TrafficClass` (existing class) – reuse for TC-1, TC-2, TC-4 individuals (already exist as `:TC_1`, `:TC_2`, `:TC_4`).
- `:AVC` (existing class) – reuse for AVC individuals.
- `:CVC` (existing class) – reuse for CVC individuals.
- `:NNIGroup` (existing class) – reuse for NNI Group individuals.
- `:POI` (existing class) – reuse for POI individuals.
- `:name` (existing datatype property) – reuse for traffic class names.
- `:sourceClause` (existing annotation property) – reuse for all new facts.

**Create New:**
- `:TrafficClassSpecification` (new class) – reification of the `hasSpecification` relationship, with properties for rate type, network point, and network type qualifiers.
- `:InformationRateType` (new class) – enumeration for CIR and PIR.
- `:InformationRateType_CIR` (new individual) – CIR rate type.
- `:InformationRateType_PIR` (new individual) – PIR rate type.
- `:NetworkPointType` (new class) – enumeration for AVC, CVC, UNI, NNI.
- `:NetworkPointType_AVC` (new individual) – AVC network point.
- `:NetworkPointType_CVC` (new individual) – CVC network point.
- `:NetworkType` (new class) – enumeration for network types (Satellite, Wireless Plus, other).
- `:NetworkType_Satellite` (new individual) – Satellite network.
- `:NetworkType_WirelessPlus` (new individual) – Wireless Plus product variant.
- `:NetworkType_Other` (new individual) – other network types.
- `:hasSpecification` (new object property) – links TrafficClass to TrafficClassSpecification.
- `:specifiesRateType` (new object property) – links TrafficClassSpecification to InformationRateType.
- `:appliesAt` (new object property) – links TrafficClassSpecification to NetworkPointType.
- `:appliesToNetwork` (new object property) – links TrafficClassSpecification to NetworkType.
- `:hasExampleApplication` (new datatype property) – links TrafficClass to example application text.
- `:alignedTo` (new datatype property) – links TrafficClass to alignment description.
- `:hasBurstCapability` (new datatype property) – links TrafficClass to burst capability description.
- `:capacitySharing` (new datatype property) – links TrafficClass to capacity sharing description.
- `:hasCapacitySharingContext` (new datatype property) – links TrafficClass to capacity sharing context (e.g., "at AVC", "at CVC for nbn Ethernet (other than Satellite)").

**Contract Facts as Individuals:**
