# Technical Implementation Plan: Access Loop Identification & Characterisation, Unicast 1:1 AVC Bandwidth Profiles

## 1) Conceptual Model & Pattern Guidance

**Concept:** `Cl_AccessLoopFeature`
**Represents:** A feature (Identification or Characterisation) that can be inserted into upstream control packets on an access loop.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Property Reification** for the `availableOn` relationship (feature × access technology × protocol × availability status). Use **Explicit Typing** to distinguish `AccessLoopIdentification` from `AccessLoopCharacterisation` as subclasses. Use **Stubs** for the protocol and access technology values (simple individuals).
**Key Relationships:** `availableOn` (reified as `AccessLoopFeatureAvailability` with `hasAccessTechnology`, `hasControlProtocol`, `hasAvailabilityStatus`); `specifiedIn` → `NetworkInterfaceSpecification_AVC`; `requiresFeature` (Characterisation requires Identification).

**Concept:** `Cl_Unicast1_1AVC`
**Represents:** An AVC bandwidth profile type comprising mandatory TC-4 and optional TC-1/TC-2 traffic classes.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Property Reification** for the `comprises` relationship (AVC type × traffic class × mandatory/optional flag). Use **Aggregation** to model the bandwidth profile as a collection of per-traffic-class upstream/downstream profiles. Use **Explicit Typing** to subclass `AVC` (reference class).
**Key Relationships:** `comprisesTrafficClass` (reified as `TrafficClassRequirement` with `isMandatory` boolean); `describedIn` → `nbnEthernetProductDescription` (Section 3.1); `availabilityByAccessTechnology` → `AccessTechnology` (reified as `AvcAvailabilityByTechnology`).

**Concept:** `Cl_AvcBandwidthProfile`
**Represents:** A valid combination of upstream/downstream bandwidth profiles for each traffic class in a Unicast 1:1 AVC.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Property Reification** for the `specifiedIn` relationship (profile × Appendix B × section B.1/B.2). Use **Aggregation** to model the profile as a collection of per-traffic-class bandwidth components. Use **Stubs** for the document section references.
**Key Relationships:** `specifiedIn` → `Appendix_B` (Sections B.1, B.2); `availabilityByAccessTechnology` → `AccessTechnology` (reified as `BandwidthProfileAvailability`); `isValidFor` → `Cl_Unicast1_1AVC`.

