## 2) Reuse & Extension Plan

**Extend/Reuse:**
- `:AVC` — reuse as superclass; `:Unicast1_1AVC` already exists as subclass (line 1441)
- `:TrafficClass` — reuse; `:TC_1`, `:TC_2`, `:TC_4` individuals already exist (lines 381-397)
- `:AccessTechnology` — reuse; `:AccessTechnology_FIBRE`, `:AccessTechnology_FTTC`, `:AccessTechnology_HFC` exist (lines 933-943)
- `:AccessNetwork_FTTB`, `:AccessNetwork_FTTN`, `:AccessNetwork_Wireless`, `:AccessNetwork_Satellite` — reuse (lines 1614-1632)
- `:DocumentSection` — reuse for `:Appendix_B` (exists, line 41) and `:NetworkInterfaceSpecification_AVC` (new)
- `:DHCPv4`, `:DHCPv6`, `:PPPoE` — reuse (lines 1636-1649)
- `:AccessLoopIdentification` — reuse (line 1459); `:AccessLoopInsertion` — reuse (line 1489)
- `:sourceClause` — reuse for all fact provenance

**Create New:**
- `:AccessLoopCharacterisation` (subclass of `:AccessLoopIdentification` or sibling) — new class
- `:AccessLoopFeatureAvailability` — reification class for feature × technology × protocol × status
- `:ControlProtocol` — new class; make `:DHCPv4`, `:DHCPv6`, `:PPPoE` instances of it
- `:AvailabilityStatus` — new class with individuals `:Available`, `:NotAvailable`
- `:TrafficClassRequirement` — reification class for AVC × traffic class × mandatory/optional
- `:AvcBandwidthProfile` — new class (distinct from `:BandwidthProfile` which is generic)
- `:BandwidthProfileComponent` — reification for per-traffic-class upstream/downstream profiles
- `:NetworkInterfaceSpecification_AVC` — new `:DocumentSection` individual
- `:nbnEthernetProductDescription` — new `:DocumentSection` individual
- `:hasAvailabilityStatus`, `:hasControlProtocol`, `:isMandatory`, `:hasUpstreamProfile`, `:hasDownstreamProfile` — new properties

**Contract Facts as Individuals:**
- One `:AccessLoopFeatureAvailability` per (feature, technology, protocol) cell in the two tables (6 technologies × 3 protocols × 2 features = 36 individuals)
- One `:TrafficClassRequirement` per traffic class in Unicast 1:1 AVC (TC-1 optional, TC-2 optional, TC-4 mandatory)
- One `:AvcBandwidthProfile` individual representing the valid profile combination
- One `:AccessLoopCharacterisation` individual with `:requiresFeature :AccessLoopIdentification_Default`

