Implementation Plan:
1) Conceptual Model & Pattern Guidance

**Concept:** `:DocumentSection`
**Represents:** A numbered section or subsection of the Wholesale Broadband Agreement document that describes a specific product component, attribute, or procedure.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Explicit Typing** (each section is an individual of `:DocumentSection`), **Name Stub** (section number and title as datatype properties), and **Tree** (parent-child hierarchy via `:hasParentSection`).
**Key Relationships:** Described by `:hasSectionNumber` and `:hasSectionTitle`; linked to product entities via `:describedInSection`; parent-child via `:hasParentSection`.

**Concept:** `:AVC` / `:CVC` / `:NNIGroup` / `:Bearer` / `:NNILink`
**Represents:** Core product components of the nbn Ethernet Product Module, each with specific service attributes and ordering procedures defined in the document.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Explicit Typing** (each is a class), **Property Reification** for n-ary relationships like `:hasServiceAttributes` (linking a product component to its attribute set and the document section), and **ParticipantRole** for ordering procedures (e.g., `:OrderingProcedure` as a role played by a `:DocumentSection`).
**Key Relationships:** `:hasServiceAttributes` (to `:ServiceAttributes`), `:hasOrderingProcedure` (to `:DocumentSection`), `:hasVariant` (for CVC variants), `:hasLocation`/`:hasInterfaceRate`/`:hasRedundancyMode` (for NNI Group attributes).

**Concept:** `:ServiceAttributes`
**Represents:** A set of service attributes for a product component, defined in a specific document section.
**Modeling Approach (ODPs):** Use **Explicit Typing** (each attribute set is an individual of a subclass of `:ServiceAttributes`), **Name Stub** (section number and title as datatype properties), and **Property Reification** to link the product component to its attribute set and the document section.
**Key Relationships:** `:describedInSection` (to `:DocumentSection`), `:hasServiceAttributes` (from product component).

2) Reuse & Extension Plan

**Extend/Reuse:**
- `:AVC` (reuse as-is)
- `:CVC` (reuse as-is; add `:hasVariant` property)
- `:NNIGroup` (reuse as-is; add `:hasLocation`, `:hasInterfaceRate`, `:hasRedundancyMode`, `:hasOrderableAttributesSummary` properties)
- `:Bearer` (reuse as-is)
- `:NNILink` (reuse as-is; covers NNI Link and V-NNI)
- `:TrafficClass` (reuse as-is; individuals `:TC_1`, `:TC_2`, `:TC_4` already exist)
- `:DocumentSection` (reuse as-is; add new individuals for sections 8.1.2.2 through 8.3.4.2 and appendices)
- `:hasSectionNumber`, `:hasSectionTitle` (reuse as-is)
- `:sourceClause` (reuse as-is)

**Create New:**
- `:UNI_D` (subclass of `:AVC`? or standalone class) – new class for UNI-D entity
- `:UNI_DSL` (subclass of `:AVC`? or standalone class) – new class for UNI-DSL entity
- `:UNI_D_ServiceAttributes` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes`) – new class for UNI-D service attributes
- `:UNI_DSL_ServiceAttributes` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes`) – new class for UNI-DSL service attributes
- `:UnicastAVC_ServiceAttributes` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes`) – new class for unicast AVC service attributes
- `:CVC_ServiceAttributes` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes`) – new class for CVC service attributes
- `:NNI_ServiceAttributes` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes`) – new class for NNI service attributes
- `:NNI_Group_Location` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes` or standalone) – new class for NNI Group Location attribute
- `:NNI_Group_InterfaceRate` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes` or standalone) – new class for NNI Group Interface Rate attribute
- `:NNI_Group_RedundancyMode` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes` or standalone) – new class for NNI Group Redundancy Mode attribute
- `:NNI_Group_OrderableAttributesSummary` (subclass of `:ServiceAttributes` or standalone) – new class for NNI Group Orderable Attributes Summary
- `:hasServiceAttributes` (object property) – links a product component to its service attributes
- `:hasVariant` (object property) – links CVC to its variant (Unicast 1:1 or Unicast N:1)
- `:hasLocation` (object property) – links NNI Group to its location attribute
- `:hasInterfaceRate` (object property) – links NNI Group to its interface rate attribute
- `:hasRedundancyMode` (object property) – links NNI Group to its redundancy mode attribute
- `:hasOrderableAttributesSummary` (object property) – links NNI Group to its orderable attributes summary
- `:hasOrderingProcedure` (object property) – links a product component to its ordering procedure document section
- `:hasModificationProcedure` (object property) – links AVC to its modification procedure document section
- `:describedInSection` (object property) – links any entity/attribute to the document section that describes it
- `:hasParentSection` (object property) – links a document section to its parent section
- New individuals for each document section listed in the CQs (sections 8.1.2.2 through 8.3.4.2, Appendix A, Appendix B)
- New individuals for each service attributes set (e.g., `:UNI_D_ServiceAttributes_8_1_2_2`, `:CVC_ServiceAttributes_8_2`, etc.)

